   "text": "This is the open-chain form of muramyl dipeptide (MDP) as its butyl ester: an N-acetylmuramic acid aldehyde, linked through its lactyl ether to L-Ala, then D-isoglutamine with a butyl ester.\n\n**Fragments read from the drawing**\n- **Butyl ester:** the four-carbon chain at the top right is bonded to O, then to C(=O) (`CCCCOC(=O)`).\n- **Isoglutamine unit:** the \u03b1-carbon carries a bold wedge to the CH2CH2C(=O)NH2 side chain and an NH to the alanine. Reading the wedge gives the D configuration.\n- **Alanine unit:** the methyl is on a hashed bond, which gives L-Ala.\n- **Lactyl ether:** the lactyl carbon has a wedged methyl and is bonded to the sugar O.\n- **Sugar chain:** it runs CHO, then C(NHAc), then C(O-lactyl), then CH(OH), then CH(OH), then CH2OH. The NHAc and the lower OH are hashed, while the O-lactyl and the upper OH are wedged.\n\nI assigned each @/@@ from the wedge/hash geometry and the order the neighbours appear in the SMILES.\n\nSMILES: CCCCOC(=O)[C@@H](CCC(N)=O)NC(=O)[C@H](C)NC(=O)[C@@H](C)O[C@H]([C@H](C=O)NC(C)=O)[C@H](O)[C@H](O)CO"
